  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "A hotel owner seeking distribution, loyalty, and operating support **without sacrificing the property’s name, design, or local character** should evaluate both soft-brand franchises and looser collection memberships.\n\n## Leading soft brands by market position\n\n| Hotel positioning | Brands worth considering | Best fit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Luxury / iconic** | **The Luxury Collection** by Marriott; **LXR Hotels & Resorts** by Hilton; **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**; **Vignette Collection** by IHG; **Emblems Collection** by Accor; **Registry Collection Hotels** by Wyndham | Landmark hotels, historic properties, luxury resorts and distinctive destination hotels. These generally preserve the hotel’s individual identity but require high luxury-service and physical-product standards. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Upper-upscale boutique / lifestyle** | **Autograph Collection** by Marriott; **Curio Collection by Hilton**; **MGallery Collection** by Accor; **WorldHotels Crafted or Elite**; **Design Hotels** | Design-led urban hotels, adaptive-reuse projects, destination resorts and properties with a compelling story. Design Hotels is particularly suitable when architecture, creativity and the owner’s vision are central to the concept. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Upscale boutique** | **Tribute Portfolio** by Marriott; **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**; **JdV by Hyatt**; **Handwritten Collection** by Accor; **Ascend Hotel Collection** by Choice | Independent upscale hotels where neighborhood character, social spaces and owner personality matter more than formal luxury positioning. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Flexible upscale or upper-midscale conversion** | **Trademark Collection by Wyndham**; **BW Premier Collection**; **BW Signature Collection** | Owners prioritizing flexible conversion, independent operation and more attainable capital requirements. Wyndham formally positions Trademark as an upper-midscale soft brand, while BWH’s collections emphasize independent operation and distinctive local character. ([development.wyndhamhotels.com](https://development.wyndhamhotels.com/upscale-lifestyle-hotel-brands/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Independent luxury membership rather than conventional franchising** | **The Leading Hotels of the World**; **Preferred Hotels & Resorts**; **WorldHotels Luxury** | Owners wanting broader sales, marketing, distribution and loyalty support while retaining greater operational independence. LHW is highly selective; Preferred offers distribution, sales, marketing and the I Prefer loyalty program. ([lhw.com](https://www.lhw.com/corporate/fact-sheet?utm_source=openai)) |\n\n## Newer options to investigate carefully\n\n- **Unscripted by Hyatt:** A newly positioned upscale collection intended for full- and focused-service hotels, emphasizing flexible design and access to World of Hyatt. It competes with Tribute, Tapestry, Ascend, Trademark and Handwritten. ([hyatt.com](https://www.hyatt.com/development/ourbrands/unscriptedbyhyatt?utm_source=openai))\n- **Noted Collection by IHG:** A premium collection designed around independently identified hotels. As of March 31, 2026, IHG reported no open hotels and one pipeline property, so owners should examine launch support and execution risk carefully. ([development.ihg.com](https://development.ihg.com/hotel-brands/premium/noted-collection?utm_source=openai))\n- **Series by Marriott:** Particularly relevant to an owner or operator with an established regional brand or portfolio, because it permits retention of the regional name while connecting hotels to Marriott Bonvoy and Marriott’s digital channels. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/seriesbymarriott?utm_source=openai))\n- **WorldHotels Backdrop:** A specialized option for upscale outdoor lodging, glamping and nature-oriented hospitality. ([development.bwhhotels.com](https://development.bwhhotels.com/content/luxury-hotels/en_US/brands.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n## Practical first-round shortlist\n\nFor a typical U.S. owner, I would initially solicit proposals as follows:\n\n### Luxury landmark or resort\n1. Luxury Collection  \n2. LXR  \n3. Unbound Collection  \n4. Vignette Collection  \n5. LHW or Preferred as the less-conventional alternative  \n\n### Upper-upscale urban boutique\n1. Autograph Collection  \n2. Curio Collection  \n3. MGallery  \n4. Unbound or JdV, depending on service level  \n5. Design Hotels  \n\n### Upscale independent conversion\n1. Tribute Portfolio  \n2. Tapestry Collection  \n3. JdV or Unscripted  \n4. Handwritten Collection  \n5. Ascend Hotel Collection  \n\n### Upper-midscale independent hotel\n1. Trademark Collection  \n2. BW Signature Collection  \n3. Ascend Hotel Collection  \n4. BW Premier Collection, if the product supports upscale positioning  \n\n## What the owner should compare\n\nThe decision should be based on **10-year net economics**, not simply brand recognition or royalty percentage:\n\n- Total royalty, marketing, reservation, loyalty and technology fees\n- Required property-improvement-plan capital\n- Expected brand-channel and loyalty contribution\n- Net ADR and occupancy improvement after all fees\n- Ability to retain the existing hotel name, website and visual identity\n- Control over design, F&B concepts, amenities and local programming\n- Mandatory systems, procurement and staffing requirements\n- Territorial protection and nearby brand saturation\n- Contract term, renewal rights, performance tests and exit damages\n- Customer-data ownership and access\n- Key money, fee ramps, conversion incentives and renovation contributions\n\n**Bottom line:** Autograph, Curio, Unbound and Vignette are strong starting points for distinctive upper-upscale or luxury assets; Tribute, Tapestry, JdV and Handwritten fit more approachable upscale boutiques; Ascend, Trademark and BWH’s collections usually deserve attention when flexibility and conversion economics are paramount. For owners who value independence above loyalty-program scale, Preferred, LHW, Design Hotels and WorldHotels should also be tested.",
